WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.525
Can you read me?

2
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.359
What do I need?

3
00:00:16.103 --> 00:00:17.275
You okay?

4
00:00:17.379 --> 00:00:19.034
I have a boyfriend.

5
00:00:19.793 --> 00:00:22.827
You've been having
a fucking affair this whole time?

6
00:00:22.852 --> 00:00:24.482
Well. we hadn't
had sex in almost a year.

7
00:00:24.586 --> 00:00:26.137
Oh. it's all my fault.

8
00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:28.137
I didn't say that.
You literally just did.

9
00:00:28.241 --> 00:00:29.655
So it didn't go well. then?

10
00:00:29.711 --> 00:00:30.758
Well. I've got all my shit

11
00:00:30.862 --> 00:00:34.034
in the back of my car. so.
as well as expected.

12
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.034
I just want you to be happy.

13
00:00:37.578 --> 00:00:39.337
It's okay to feel lost.

14
00:00:40.137 --> 00:00:44.172
Sometimes it clears the path
for new things to happen.

15
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:52.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

16
00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:22.344
So...

17
00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:24.000
this is the date.

18
00:01:24.103 --> 00:01:25.655
I love that.

19
00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.241
Do we have a game plan?

20
00:01:30.344 --> 00:01:34.206
Listen. I've got a list.
but I am prone to impulse.

21
00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.110
We could end up with a
lot of spontaneous purchases.

22
00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:38.457
Do you need me
to rein you in?

23
00:01:38.482 --> 00:01:39.931
Just so I know
the ground rules here.

24
00:01:40.034 --> 00:01:41.428
I mean. you can try.

25
00:01:41.482 --> 00:01:43.147
You'll never convince me
in the moment. though.

26
00:01:43.172 --> 00:01:45.413
Everything is an amazing idea.

27
00:01:47.241 --> 00:01:49.724
Ah. no thanks.

28
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.310
Mike says "Fucking great..."

29
00:01:59.523 --> 00:02:00.583
What is?

30
00:02:01.724 --> 00:02:03.482
Do you have reception?

31
00:02:05.965 --> 00:02:07.176
Just gone to no bars.

32
00:02:07.203 --> 00:02:09.034
Oh. man.

33
00:02:09.137 --> 00:02:11.034
Do you think they do this
on purpose?

34
00:02:11.453 --> 00:02:14.760
What. create huge shells of metal
and concrete to block reception

35
00:02:14.793 --> 00:02:16.902
so you can't look at your phone
and compare prices?

36
00:02:17.229 --> 00:02:18.329
Probably.

37
00:02:19.068 --> 00:02:20.241
They do have free Wi-Fi.

38
00:02:20.344 --> 00:02:22.103
Ew. I don't use public Wi-Fi.

39
00:02:22.206 --> 00:02:23.856
You don't use public Wi-Fi. do you?

40
00:02:23.882 --> 00:02:24.931
It's free.

41
00:02:25.034 --> 00:02:27.965
Public Wi-Fi is like public toilets.

42
00:02:28.068 --> 00:02:29.758
You stay out.

43
00:02:31.482 --> 00:02:33.827
Oh. you don't use public toilets too.
do you?

44
00:02:33.931 --> 00:02:36.448
Of course.
But guys don't have to sit down.

45
00:02:36.551 --> 00:02:39.610
No surface contact.
What a charmed life you lead.

46
00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.413
Ooh. cutlery.

47
00:02:42.517 --> 00:02:44.448
Fifteen bucks.

48
00:02:45.413 --> 00:02:46.413
Done.

49
00:02:52.724 --> 00:02:54.137
Do you think this couch is me?

50
00:02:54.241 --> 00:02:56.379
Could be. Might be.

51
00:02:56.482 --> 00:02:58.448
You never know until you try it.

52
00:03:00.517 --> 00:03:03.015
I think that pineapple is staring at you.

53
00:03:03.128 --> 00:03:04.137
Yeah.

54
00:03:06.551 --> 00:03:08.144
Do you owe him money or something?

55
00:03:09.724 --> 00:03:11.451
Hey. don't stare.

56
00:03:12.137 --> 00:03:15.068
I'm so sorry. He's got ADHD.

57
00:03:15.172 --> 00:03:17.517
It's fine. I'm a big fan of pineapple.

58
00:03:17.542 --> 00:03:18.840
It has a lot of health benefits.

59
00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.539
They had a back-to-school dress-up day.
but. um...

60
00:03:22.852 --> 00:03:24.456
it was supposed to be job-themed.

61
00:03:24.489 --> 00:03:26.329
Do you want to be a pineapple
when you grow up?

62
00:03:26.413 --> 00:03:28.931
No. the suit's from last year's fruit day.

63
00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:31.454
Uh. he didn't want to be
the only kid not dressing up

64
00:03:31.527 --> 00:03:33.551
but. um. he doesn't know
what he wants to be.

65
00:03:33.965 --> 00:03:35.758
It's okay. None of us do.

66
00:03:35.862 --> 00:03:37.689
There are worse things
to be than a pineapple.

67
00:03:38.103 --> 00:03:39.510
I believe you could do it.

68
00:03:41.298 --> 00:03:42.344
Say "Bye".

69
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.509
Oh.

70
00:03:48.931 --> 00:03:50.448
Can we stay here forever?

71
00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:52.590
No.

72
00:03:52.616 --> 00:03:54.590
Come on.

73
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.517
Everyone has ADHD these days.

74
00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:02.512
Is anyone still just
a rude. weird arsehole?

75
00:04:02.732 --> 00:04:04.758
Are you calling that little pineapple
an arsehole?

76
00:04:04.862 --> 00:04:07.068
No. he was cute enough.

77
00:04:07.172 --> 00:04:09.793
But let him be weird and awkward
and see what happens.

78
00:04:09.896 --> 00:04:11.448
He could turn out to be really fun.

79
00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.827
These are very nice.

80
00:04:14.827 --> 00:04:17.137
18 pieces for 40 bucks.

81
00:04:17.241 --> 00:04:18.758
That is very good.

82
00:04:18.862 --> 00:04:21.241
Should I get 2?
For dinner parties?

83
00:04:21.284 --> 00:04:22.448
How many friends do you have?

84
00:04:22.551 --> 00:04:23.932
I don't have any friends.

85
00:04:24.586 --> 00:04:25.689
But I use all my dishes

86
00:04:25.793 --> 00:04:27.000
and I like clean things.

87
00:04:27.103 --> 00:04:29.344
I just don't like cleaning things.

88
00:04:30.896 --> 00:04:32.430
That sounded pathetic.

89
00:04:32.931 --> 00:04:34.586
I'm not a loser. okay?

90
00:04:34.689 --> 00:04:36.206
I have friends...

91
00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:37.557
I think.

92
00:04:38.965 --> 00:04:40.491
How many friends do you have?

93
00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:43.206
Let me see. Ahh. none.

94
00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.679
I don't have any friends.

95
00:04:45.137 --> 00:04:46.275
Really?

96
00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:49.984
I mean. I used to have a drink
with people from school once a year

97
00:04:50.038 --> 00:04:51.423
and work friends like Helen.

98
00:04:51.448 --> 00:04:53.206
But now I don't really hang out
with anyone.

99
00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.883
Yeah. me neither.

100
00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:56.930
Are we losers?

101
00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.758
I mean. I don't really feel like a loser.
Do you?

102
00:05:00.862 --> 00:05:02.586
Yes. I do.

103
00:05:02.689 --> 00:05:04.241
How do we not have any friends?

104
00:05:04.344 --> 00:05:05.689
We're amazing people.

105
00:05:05.793 --> 00:05:07.760
I would love to be friends with us.

106
00:05:23.123 --> 00:05:24.586
This article says that millennials

107
00:05:24.689 --> 00:05:27.379
have the least amount of friends
of all the generations.

108
00:05:27.482 --> 00:05:29.068
What did you search?

109
00:05:29.448 --> 00:05:30.758
'Why don't I have any friends?'

110
00:05:30.862 --> 00:05:32.310
Are you getting a signal?

111
00:05:32.406 --> 00:05:33.820
I'm on the Wi-Fi.

112
00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:39.034
'27% of millennials have no close friends.'

113
00:05:39.137 --> 00:05:40.931
'30% have no best friend.'

114
00:05:41.034 --> 00:05:43.448
'20% report having no friends at all.'

115
00:05:43.793 --> 00:05:45.482
We're like the worst segment of that.

116
00:05:45.586 --> 00:05:49.862
'Overall. 30% of millennials report
feeling often or always lonely.

117
00:05:49.965 --> 00:05:52.896
significantly higher than
other generations.'

118
00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.310
Wow.

119
00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.448
Do you feel lonely?

120
00:05:58.241 --> 00:05:59.310
Yeah

121
00:05:59.827 --> 00:06:01.275
I do

122
00:06:02.776 --> 00:06:04.150
sometimes.

123
00:06:05.793 --> 00:06:07.758
Ooh. spatula.

124
00:06:07.862 --> 00:06:09.758
A dollar fifty.

125
00:06:09.862 --> 00:06:12.401
Or I could get 2 for 6 dollars.

126
00:06:12.441 --> 00:06:13.474
As an accountant...

127
00:06:13.517 --> 00:06:15.896
I mean. it's more but you get two.

128
00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.275
That's 2 meals
before I have to do the dishes.

129
00:06:18.379 --> 00:06:19.970
Well why not 2 of the cheap ones?

130
00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.517
Well.

131
00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.310
these ones have solid acacia wood handles.

132
00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:26.517
Is that good?

133
00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:28.137
Sounds good.

134
00:06:28.344 --> 00:06:30.586
Well. it sounds like you
already know what you want.

135
00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:33.586
Hey. I'm cheap.
but I'm easily swayed.

136
00:06:33.688 --> 00:06:35.456
And these could end as your spatulas too.

137
00:06:35.481 --> 00:06:36.896
if you play your cards right.

138
00:06:37.448 --> 00:06:39.172
Well. I love the wood ones.

139
00:06:39.517 --> 00:06:41.551
Really? Me too.

140
00:06:41.655 --> 00:06:43.241
Good choice.

141
00:06:45.862 --> 00:06:49.402
How is this display bed
so much nicer than mine?

142
00:06:50.172 --> 00:06:52.862
Well. next payday. I'm getting a new bed

143
00:06:53.517 --> 00:06:55.310
or a deposit on one.

144
00:06:56.689 --> 00:06:58.655
Are you a spooner?

145
00:06:58.758 --> 00:07:00.484
Do you need me to be?
No.

146
00:07:00.833 --> 00:07:02.410
I never turn my back on anybody.

147
00:07:02.435 --> 00:07:03.783
That's how they get you.

148
00:07:03.832 --> 00:07:05.251
Good.

149
00:07:06.258 --> 00:07:08.862
I'm more of a 'turn and meet in the middle'
kind of guy.

150
00:07:12.689 --> 00:07:15.243
Ahh. this is nice. right?

151
00:07:18.068 --> 00:07:20.379
Do real people actually spoon?

152
00:07:20.931 --> 00:07:23.965
I'm sure some people do somewhere.

153
00:07:24.448 --> 00:07:27.517
We've been swapping left and right
these past few weeks.

154
00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.689
What side do you naturally sleep on?

155
00:07:30.103 --> 00:07:32.157
Traditionally I fall on the left.

156
00:07:32.217 --> 00:07:34.357
Uh oh. Me too.

157
00:07:34.689 --> 00:07:36.517
Well. flip you for it?

158
00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.758
Do you have a coin?
I have an app.

159
00:07:40.082 --> 00:07:41.424
Installed?
Mmm hmm.

160
00:07:41.449 --> 00:07:42.497
How often do you use that?

161
00:07:42.551 --> 00:07:45.413
Oh. you'd be surprised
how often I use it.

162
00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.068
Okay.

163
00:07:47.655 --> 00:07:49.586
Heads or tails?
Tails.

164
00:07:49.689 --> 00:07:51.206
Interesting.

165
00:07:52.137 --> 00:07:54.517
Ahh... oh.

166
00:07:55.448 --> 00:07:56.827
My phone died.

167
00:07:56.931 --> 00:07:58.551
Didn't you charge it on the way?

168
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.137
Hey. this is my workhorse.

169
00:08:01.241 --> 00:08:04.034
Texts. emails. notes. research.

170
00:08:04.137 --> 00:08:05.910
My entire life is on this thing.

171
00:08:06.551 --> 00:08:08.310
and I forgot to charge it last night.

172
00:08:09.724 --> 00:08:11.148
How often do you charge yours?

173
00:08:11.508 --> 00:08:12.793
Like. once every couple of days.

174
00:08:12.861 --> 00:08:13.862
Wow.

175
00:08:13.965 --> 00:08:15.241
What a life you live.

176
00:08:15.328 --> 00:08:16.354
It's okay.

177
00:08:16.401 --> 00:08:17.517
I have a charger.

178
00:08:26.182 --> 00:08:27.195
Dead?

179
00:08:27.535 --> 00:08:29.223
I forgot to charge the charger.

180
00:08:30.965 --> 00:08:32.551
Okay. let's keep it moving.

181
00:08:34.047 --> 00:08:35.110
Still no reception.

182
00:08:35.203 --> 00:08:37.586
Oh. This is like a horror movie.

183
00:08:37.689 --> 00:08:40.344
Big maze. No phone signal.

184
00:08:40.448 --> 00:08:42.827
You should have listened to the
old man at the gas station.

185
00:08:42.931 --> 00:08:46.482
Hmm. he did say a lot of people
go missing around these parts.

186
00:08:46.586 --> 00:08:48.068
Pull yourself together. Focus.

187
00:08:48.172 --> 00:08:50.946
We've got to get to higher ground
to see if we can get a signal.

188
00:08:51.012 --> 00:08:52.106
Come on.

189
00:09:17.367 --> 00:09:18.368
Rrrahh!

190
00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.931
Oh... God!

191
00:09:20.034 --> 00:09:22.172
You idiot!

192
00:09:22.275 --> 00:09:24.103
But I'm your idiot.

193
00:09:25.758 --> 00:09:28.758
I like this. but I don't see
the bin in this colour.

194
00:09:29.378 --> 00:09:31.275
Why don't you just get a
different coloured bin?

195
00:09:31.379 --> 00:09:33.620
Have you been paying
any attention to my cart?

196
00:09:33.724 --> 00:09:35.623
I've got a colour scheme
going on here.

197
00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:38.084
Change of plans.

198
00:09:38.264 --> 00:09:39.329
What about black?

199
00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.619
Do you see your toothbrush parked
in a black toothbrush holder?

200
00:09:43.241 --> 00:09:45.034
The black is a bit too intense.

201
00:09:45.137 --> 00:09:46.413
What about the aqua one?

202
00:09:47.392 --> 00:09:48.782
It's turquoise. but...

203
00:09:48.876 --> 00:09:51.567
yeah. I like it. Good choice.

204
00:09:51.592 --> 00:09:53.159
But now we have to redo
the whole thing.

205
00:09:53.199 --> 00:09:54.759
Do you even need a bin in the bathroom?

206
00:09:54.786 --> 00:09:56.772
Do you know anything about women?

207
00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:59.689
You're really throwing up
red flags here. dude.

208
00:10:01.965 --> 00:10:04.137
'Red flags to look for when
dating a new man.'

209
00:10:04.241 --> 00:10:05.620
Hmm. this should be good.

210
00:10:05.724 --> 00:10:08.206
'He's over 30 and still
lives with his parents.'

211
00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:10.379
Technicality: grandparents

212
00:10:10.404 --> 00:10:11.423
or is that worse?

213
00:10:11.448 --> 00:10:12.215
I don't think so.

214
00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:14.172
I think you've got
a pretty sweet setup going on.

215
00:10:14.275 --> 00:10:16.344
It's kind of separate
from the main house.

216
00:10:16.448 --> 00:10:18.103
I give you a pass on this one.

217
00:10:18.206 --> 00:10:19.756
Well. thank you.
Hmm.

218
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.827
When was this quiz written. 1980?

219
00:10:23.931 --> 00:10:26.172
I can barely afford the rent
on this new place.

220
00:10:26.275 --> 00:10:29.543
If that's a red flag.
then we are all fucked in this economy.

221
00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:32.620
'He seems a little too perfect.'

222
00:10:32.827 --> 00:10:34.310
We'll see.

223
00:10:36.482 --> 00:10:38.758
'He promotes an alpha attitude.'

224
00:10:39.303 --> 00:10:40.317
Uhh. uhh.

225
00:10:40.793 --> 00:10:42.620
'He spends more time
with his friends.'

226
00:10:42.724 --> 00:10:45.103
Oh God. they're really digging
in the boot. huh?

227
00:10:45.206 --> 00:10:46.510
Pass.

228
00:10:49.448 --> 00:10:50.793
Uhh. are you allowed to do that?

229
00:10:50.896 --> 00:10:51.935
Well. it's not stealing.

230
00:10:51.965 --> 00:10:53.875
It's going to be mine in 20 minutes.

231
00:10:56.586 --> 00:10:58.226
'He is not emotionally open.'

232
00:10:58.553 --> 00:11:00.724
See. I don't really get that.
What does that even mean?

233
00:11:00.827 --> 00:11:03.596
Oh. I think it just means
you're forthcoming

234
00:11:03.623 --> 00:11:05.250
and honest about your feelings.

235
00:11:05.328 --> 00:11:08.137
I mean. I feel like I've been pretty honest
with you so far. haven't I?

236
00:11:08.241 --> 00:11:10.496
Yeah. you have. As far as I know.

237
00:11:11.151 --> 00:11:14.005
Did you want me to tell you
every single thing that I'm feeling

238
00:11:14.058 --> 00:11:15.793
because I've done the open
book thing before

239
00:11:15.896 --> 00:11:17.456
and it's never really worked out.

240
00:11:17.556 --> 00:11:18.636
That's interesting.

241
00:11:18.827 --> 00:11:20.379
Unpack that for me.

242
00:11:20.816 --> 00:11:23.551
I mean. I do this thing where
I understand people pretty quickly

243
00:11:23.655 --> 00:11:27.803
and when I express my observations
in an open-hearted way.

244
00:11:27.876 --> 00:11:28.892
they tend to get mad.

245
00:11:29.931 --> 00:11:31.066
It doesn't really sound like

246
00:11:31.091 --> 00:11:33.724
you're being emotionally
honest about yourself. though.

247
00:11:33.827 --> 00:11:36.544
It sort of just sounds like
you're talking at people.

248
00:11:36.584 --> 00:11:39.486
which sort of sounds a bit rude.

249
00:11:40.697 --> 00:11:41.877
Noted.

250
00:11:45.724 --> 00:11:48.896
'He is over 30 and never had
a long-term relationship.'

251
00:11:49.019 --> 00:11:50.672
Ooh. Go!

252
00:11:50.733 --> 00:11:52.644
What was your longest relationship?

253
00:11:52.677 --> 00:11:53.689
Five years.

254
00:11:53.793 --> 00:11:55.000
Wait. what?

255
00:11:55.103 --> 00:11:56.172
When?

256
00:11:56.275 --> 00:11:57.965
25 to 30.

257
00:11:58.448 --> 00:11:59.863
What happened?

258
00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:01.965
It kind of just played itself out.

259
00:12:02.068 --> 00:12:05.000
Oh. come on. you have to give me
more than that.

260
00:12:05.862 --> 00:12:07.448
What was she like?

261
00:12:07.551 --> 00:12:09.137
What was her name?

262
00:12:09.241 --> 00:12:11.250
Did you ever get engaged
at any point?

263
00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.263
Come on. You have to give me something.

264
00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.078
Her name was Sam.
Mmm.

265
00:12:15.103 --> 00:12:18.000
And she was great. It wasn't her fault.

266
00:12:18.103 --> 00:12:19.889
And no. we were never engaged.

267
00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:21.156
How?

268
00:12:21.376 --> 00:12:24.137
Sorry. This is none of my business.

269
00:12:24.241 --> 00:12:26.443
No. It's fine. I just never really asked.

270
00:12:27.551 --> 00:12:29.636
It shouldn't have gone on
for as long as it did.

271
00:12:31.137 --> 00:12:33.368
I... I knew it wasn't really going to last.

272
00:12:33.395 --> 00:12:35.068
and it wasn't really fair on her.

273
00:12:35.724 --> 00:12:36.931
How'd you know?

274
00:12:37.586 --> 00:12:39.206
I mean. you just know. right?

275
00:12:40.383 --> 00:12:41.696
Yep.

276
00:12:43.172 --> 00:12:45.827
Okay. So. longest relationship.

277
00:12:45.857 --> 00:12:46.897
No.

278
00:12:47.103 --> 00:12:49.931
Excuse me. this is
a 'red flags for dudes' quiz.

279
00:12:49.957 --> 00:12:50.957
Fair's fair.

280
00:12:53.758 --> 00:12:55.344
Okay. fine.

281
00:12:55.448 --> 00:12:57.965
Two years with David.

282
00:12:58.068 --> 00:12:59.356
But by circumstance.

283
00:12:59.403 --> 00:13:01.883
We got a little locked in
by the old pandemic.

284
00:13:02.827 --> 00:13:04.137
And what about before that?

285
00:13:04.965 --> 00:13:06.000
Hmm...

286
00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.413
I guess just a couple of months.

287
00:13:08.463 --> 00:13:09.482
Really?

288
00:13:09.517 --> 00:13:10.517
A couple of months.

289
00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:11.827
Is that it?

290
00:13:12.965 --> 00:13:15.241
Wait. am I the red flag here?

291
00:13:23.793 --> 00:13:26.683
'He avoids talk of commitment
and remains elusive about the future.'

292
00:13:26.716 --> 00:13:29.413
Well. I did ask you to marry me. didn't I?

293
00:13:29.517 --> 00:13:31.330
But that has been a problem in the past.

294
00:13:32.896 --> 00:13:35.670
David asked me to marry him after a year.

295
00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:37.620
Really?
Mmm hmm.

296
00:13:37.724 --> 00:13:39.656
And what was your answer?
Nothing.

297
00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:42.517
I just ran to the bathroom and
he never brought it up again.

298
00:13:43.137 --> 00:13:44.793
'He has a history of cheating.'

299
00:13:44.896 --> 00:13:46.884
Never.
Never?

300
00:13:47.379 --> 00:13:50.620
Hmm. Pass. obviously.

301
00:13:50.724 --> 00:13:52.736
But never before.

302
00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.310
Have you ever been cheated on?

303
00:13:55.413 --> 00:13:57.551
Nope. Or. I don't think so.

304
00:13:57.655 --> 00:13:58.758
Not that I know of.

305
00:13:58.862 --> 00:13:59.965
I have.

306
00:14:00.068 --> 00:14:01.482
Well. I'm not gonna do that.

307
00:14:01.586 --> 00:14:03.620
Yeah. that's what they all say.

308
00:14:03.724 --> 00:14:05.403
Yeah. but I'm not them. I'm me.

309
00:14:06.236 --> 00:14:08.092
You know. I didn't even have
a proper boyfriend

310
00:14:08.117 --> 00:14:09.172
until after high school.

311
00:14:09.197 --> 00:14:10.335
I find that hard to believe.

312
00:14:10.379 --> 00:14:11.931
Well. believe it.

313
00:14:12.034 --> 00:14:14.241
And when I did. I got the big fish.

314
00:14:14.344 --> 00:14:16.103
The most popular guy at school.

315
00:14:16.206 --> 00:14:17.379
Captain of the football team?

316
00:14:18.166 --> 00:14:19.172
No.

317
00:14:19.197 --> 00:14:20.610
The thing about my school was that

318
00:14:20.635 --> 00:14:22.344
 the douchebags were the cool kids.

319
00:14:23.262 --> 00:14:25.413
Ugh. it was so dumb.

320
00:14:25.517 --> 00:14:28.028
I was just so over the moon
that he had picked me.

321
00:14:28.128 --> 00:14:29.689
that somebody had picked me.

322
00:14:30.517 --> 00:14:32.344
I'd been a real nobody at school.

323
00:14:32.448 --> 00:14:33.758
Come on.
No. it's true.

324
00:14:33.862 --> 00:14:35.586
Anyone will tell you.

325
00:14:35.689 --> 00:14:38.137
And they'll tell you how lucky I was.

326
00:14:38.241 --> 00:14:39.403
And I believed it.

327
00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.810
and I was somebody for. like. three months.

328
00:14:43.827 --> 00:14:46.241
and he was cheating on me the entire time.

329
00:14:46.344 --> 00:14:47.595
and everyone knew.

330
00:14:48.034 --> 00:14:51.344
And they still said I was lucky
because I was the public girlfriend.

331
00:14:51.448 --> 00:14:53.344
How fucked up is that?

332
00:14:53.448 --> 00:14:55.586
It's up there.
Hmm.

333
00:14:55.689 --> 00:14:57.689
And it was with my sister.

334
00:14:57.793 --> 00:14:59.196
What?
Mmm hmm.

335
00:14:59.724 --> 00:15:01.103
Yeah. I come from a town

336
00:15:01.206 --> 00:15:04.206
where everyone fucks everyone
and nobody gets out alive.

337
00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:05.827
Except you.

338
00:15:05.931 --> 00:15:07.363
Did I. though?

339
00:15:10.282 --> 00:15:11.448
Do you still talk to her?

340
00:15:11.551 --> 00:15:13.103
Not if I can avoid it.

341
00:15:13.206 --> 00:15:14.275
A couple of times a year.

342
00:15:14.379 --> 00:15:16.902
Five minutes on birthdays and things.

343
00:15:17.551 --> 00:15:19.415
They have a kid now.
They?

344
00:15:20.241 --> 00:15:23.620
Yeah. they're still together.
They're married.

345
00:15:23.751 --> 00:15:25.889
Holy shit.
Yeah.

346
00:15:25.965 --> 00:15:28.068
Ah. it's fine though.

347
00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:29.990
They were built for that place.

348
00:15:30.379 --> 00:15:33.931
I dodged a bullet.
and they seem happy. I think.

349
00:15:34.034 --> 00:15:35.551
But still.
Yeah.

350
00:15:35.655 --> 00:15:36.783
But still.

351
00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:40.303
All right.

352
00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:43.620
'He's a serial dater with little
or no gaps between relationships.'

353
00:15:43.749 --> 00:15:44.758
Okay. you know what?

354
00:15:44.862 --> 00:15:46.862
This quiz is fucking stupid.

355
00:15:46.971 --> 00:15:52.245
If everyone used this as a yardstick
to decide and define their relationships

356
00:15:52.412 --> 00:15:55.952
 it's no wonder everyone
is alone and miserable.

357
00:15:56.215 --> 00:15:57.931
I mean. who can pass this shit?

358
00:15:58.034 --> 00:16:00.344
We failed half of this stupid quiz.

359
00:16:00.448 --> 00:16:01.744
And yet. here we are.

360
00:16:03.034 --> 00:16:04.164
Here we are.

361
00:16:07.241 --> 00:16:08.310
Ahh. fuck 'em.

362
00:16:12.896 --> 00:16:14.931
28... 29.

363
00:16:21.344 --> 00:16:23.116
This one.
35.

364
00:16:23.413 --> 00:16:25.463
'Grönsta!'
Oh!

365
00:16:27.896 --> 00:16:29.517
Dang. it's heavy.

366
00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:34.680
Thank you.
You're welcome.

367
00:16:41.216 --> 00:16:43.000
Woo-hoo!

368
00:16:44.931 --> 00:16:46.862
So this is my shout.

369
00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:50.356
This is the best date ever.

370
00:16:52.965 --> 00:16:55.448
So I've been making my way
through your reviews and articles.

371
00:16:55.551 --> 00:16:57.508
Uh oh.
Very funny.

372
00:16:58.310 --> 00:16:59.620
Thank you.

373
00:16:59.724 --> 00:17:02.793
No. I knew you were. like. funny
in real life and everything. but

374
00:17:03.068 --> 00:17:05.206
you're a great writer too.

375
00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.344
That's very nice of you.

376
00:17:07.448 --> 00:17:08.931
And I read your short story.

377
00:17:09.034 --> 00:17:10.206
Wait. what?

378
00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:12.551
My short story? How did you...?

379
00:17:12.827 --> 00:17:14.689
Have you been cyberstalking me?

380
00:17:14.793 --> 00:17:15.965
Yeah. you inspired me.

381
00:17:16.068 --> 00:17:17.931
Did you not trawl
through my social media

382
00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.655
and find out everything
you could about me?

383
00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:20.710
Fair enough.

384
00:17:21.487 --> 00:17:23.413
I didn't know you were an
award-winning author.

385
00:17:23.517 --> 00:17:25.620
Second place.

386
00:17:25.724 --> 00:17:27.682
Did you get a trophy?
I got a certificate.

387
00:17:28.308 --> 00:17:29.768
That's an award.

388
00:17:30.375 --> 00:17:31.682
Hi.

389
00:17:33.206 --> 00:17:34.931
The whole contest folded a year later.

390
00:17:35.034 --> 00:17:36.956
I think the bar was getting pretty low.

391
00:17:37.776 --> 00:17:39.010
We're good?

392
00:17:39.229 --> 00:17:40.237
Thank you.

393
00:17:40.262 --> 00:17:41.269
Thanks.

394
00:17:42.086 --> 00:17:43.369
I loved it.

395
00:17:44.655 --> 00:17:46.337
'And the air was filled with coconut smoke

396
00:17:46.397 --> 00:17:49.020
and the dense tang of
a hundred clashing fragrances.'

397
00:17:49.047 --> 00:17:50.068
Oh.

398
00:17:50.172 --> 00:17:51.586
That's my favorite line.

399
00:17:51.689 --> 00:17:53.310
Thank you.

400
00:17:53.413 --> 00:17:56.379
You get paid to do what you do.
which would stand to reason

401
00:17:56.482 --> 00:17:58.413
that you're good at it. Right?

402
00:17:59.216 --> 00:18:00.275
You're really good at it.

403
00:18:00.379 --> 00:18:02.275
Okay... Is this going to be

404
00:18:02.379 --> 00:18:05.344
one of those 'you're too good
for what you're doing' things?

405
00:18:05.448 --> 00:18:06.698
No.

406
00:18:06.738 --> 00:18:09.655
I'm just letting you know that I
think you're great at what you do.

407
00:18:10.327 --> 00:18:11.410
Thank you.

408
00:18:19.034 --> 00:18:22.655
So. are you good at accounting?

409
00:18:23.068 --> 00:18:25.551
Yep. But I'm not gonna make you
read a bunch of spreadsheets.

410
00:18:28.551 --> 00:18:30.517
What you do is quantifiable.

411
00:18:31.482 --> 00:18:33.409
Entertaining talent. People like that.

412
00:18:42.198 --> 00:18:43.922
I almost had one of those.

413
00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.310
Had one what?

414
00:18:46.413 --> 00:18:48.413
A kid.

415
00:18:48.526 --> 00:18:49.595
Really?

416
00:18:49.965 --> 00:18:51.418
Right at the start of lockdown.

417
00:18:51.645 --> 00:18:52.725
Oh.

418
00:18:52.811 --> 00:18:53.824
Yeah.

419
00:18:53.878 --> 00:18:55.620
I was probably pregnant
last time I saw you.

420
00:18:55.724 --> 00:18:57.413
and I didn't even know it yet.

421
00:18:57.445 --> 00:18:58.446
Oh. wow.

422
00:18:58.486 --> 00:18:59.539
Yeah.

423
00:18:59.931 --> 00:19:02.470
Good thing that you didn't
hit on me then. huh?

424
00:19:05.209 --> 00:19:06.265
What happened?

425
00:19:07.118 --> 00:19:09.770
Err. it didn't take.

426
00:19:10.448 --> 00:19:12.551
I miscarried after 15 weeks.

427
00:19:12.655 --> 00:19:14.427
I've got a septate uterus.

428
00:19:14.452 --> 00:19:15.452
A what?

429
00:19:15.492 --> 00:19:17.756
Ah. my uterus is like a nose.

430
00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.517
It has a septum running
through the middle.

431
00:19:21.103 --> 00:19:23.137
Wow. Never heard of that before.

432
00:19:23.241 --> 00:19:24.843
Yeah. neither had I.

433
00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.241
But I'm hopefully getting it fixed

434
00:19:28.344 --> 00:19:30.312
now that elective surgeries are back on.

435
00:19:30.337 --> 00:19:30.931
So don't worry.

436
00:19:31.034 --> 00:19:31.824
You're not going to be saddled

437
00:19:31.904 --> 00:19:34.364
with some vaginal freak show or something.

438
00:19:39.656 --> 00:19:42.583
I did ask the doctor
if I could ever have kids.

439
00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:44.586
and he said. 'We'll see.'

440
00:19:45.172 --> 00:19:48.758
That's a very poor thing
to carry around at 35.

441
00:19:50.241 --> 00:19:51.275
I'm sorry.

442
00:19:51.379 --> 00:19:52.827
Mmm.
That that happened to you.

443
00:19:52.931 --> 00:19:54.379
It is what it is.

444
00:19:54.482 --> 00:19:57.034
That's what they say. right?

445
00:19:58.019 --> 00:19:59.606
Something like that.

446
00:20:05.793 --> 00:20:06.903
Can I be honest?

447
00:20:08.377 --> 00:20:11.276
This is such a horrible
thing to say. but...

448
00:20:11.562 --> 00:20:13.543
I was actually kind of relieved.

449
00:20:14.724 --> 00:20:15.758
How did David take it?

450
00:20:15.862 --> 00:20:19.551
Very cavalier. very pragmatic.

451
00:20:19.873 --> 00:20:22.079
I mean. he is a doctor after all.

452
00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:24.379
He was like. 'It's okay.'

453
00:20:24.482 --> 00:20:27.517
'Just wasn't meant to be.'

454
00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:33.275
And I was. like. 'This whole
fucking thing isn't meant to be.'

455
00:20:33.575 --> 00:20:35.610
And I knew there and then.

456
00:20:35.827 --> 00:20:37.270
I think he did too.

457
00:20:37.766 --> 00:20:39.570
But we stayed in it anyway.

458
00:20:41.413 --> 00:20:44.076
I've always been really scared
of being alone.

459
00:20:44.896 --> 00:20:46.827
And then the pandemic hit.
and suddenly

460
00:20:46.931 --> 00:20:49.110
everyone is isolated.

461
00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:53.730
I mean. I didn't even see anyone really.

462
00:20:53.777 --> 00:20:56.516
 other than David for. like. 2 years.

463
00:20:57.551 --> 00:20:59.482
And so I was scared of leaving him

464
00:20:59.586 --> 00:21:01.776
because I didn't want to be truly alone.

465
00:21:02.252 --> 00:21:05.252
But I was still lonely

466
00:21:05.633 --> 00:21:07.350
even when I was with him.

467
00:21:10.965 --> 00:21:12.620
After we lost the baby.

468
00:21:12.724 --> 00:21:15.586
I don't think either of us
wanted to lose anything else.

469
00:21:18.896 --> 00:21:22.379
I don't think human beings are
meant to be stuck at home alone.

470
00:21:22.482 --> 00:21:24.296
I think we're meant to be out in the world.

471
00:21:24.506 --> 00:21:25.736
living.

472
00:21:26.758 --> 00:21:29.068
eating meatballs at IKEA.

473
00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.586
The kid would be. like. over a year now.

474
00:21:38.272 --> 00:21:41.163
I mean. can you imagine me with a kid?

475
00:21:41.241 --> 00:21:44.323
I can barely take care of myself.

476
00:21:45.275 --> 00:21:46.290
Em.

477
00:21:47.213 --> 00:21:48.237
Come here.

478
00:22:00.344 --> 00:22:02.931
Well. yeah. there's the story.

479
00:22:03.034 --> 00:22:06.503
There's your out. if any of that
is a dealbreaker for you.

480
00:22:07.379 --> 00:22:08.915
It's not a dealbreaker for me.

481
00:22:10.793 --> 00:22:12.068
Even after all that?

482
00:22:12.172 --> 00:22:13.761
Especially after all that.

483
00:22:15.103 --> 00:22:17.516
As far as skeletons go.
you're doing fine.

484
00:22:32.379 --> 00:22:33.476
Sorry.

485
00:22:38.643 --> 00:22:39.890
What's up?

486
00:22:42.241 --> 00:22:45.137
Antonio quit as CEO

487
00:22:45.241 --> 00:22:49.862
and his company just shut down
the entire online publishing section.

488
00:22:55.896 --> 00:22:57.703
I think I just lost my job.

488
00:22:58.305 --> 00:23:58.380
